    "overview": {
      "body": "The deep erg offers broad exposed working ground and few sheltered alternatives. Survey the actual substrate around a proposed camp or work site before relying on it as refuge."
    },
    "settlement": {
      "body": "Limited rock and sparse wild resources make collection, storage and retreat harder to arrange. Keep essential rooms enclosed and place supplies where a withdrawing party can reach them."
    },
    "wormCountry": {
      "body": "Footsteps, harvesting and machinery disturb the sand. The scarcity of rock makes early withdrawal especially important; laying a floor over the dunes does not create natural worm safety."
    }
  },
